TuneThatHue is freeware: it costs nothing, it has no licence key and no paid tier.
Freeware does not mean that the source is free to change or to copy; the terms below say
what you may do.

1. Scope. This licence covers the TuneThatHue software and materials published by the
   licensor (the "Software"): the daemon and its web page, the QNAP package, the Windows,
   macOS and Linux installers, the sender plug-ins and programs (Winamp, foobar2000, AIMP,
   Sound Capture), the container image, and its scripts, texts, images, icons and videos.
   It does not cover third-party components. Each of those keeps its own licence, listed
   in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, and nothing here limits the rights those licences give you.
   A file or directory that names another licence (in its header, a COPYING file or its
   own LICENSE file) is under that licence: effects/ holds Music Assistant's code under
   the Apache License 2.0 (effects/LICENSE).

2. Use. You may install and run the Software, free of charge, on any number of devices
   that you own or administer (QNAP NAS units, computers, Raspberry Pi boards), for
   private or business purposes. You may configure it, change its settings and keep your
   own data in it. That is not modification.

